# .trivyignore — reviewed CVE exceptions for the ContentRemixer security gate
# (ISI-7120 / C2, plan §2 job 8). Trivy reads this file for BOTH the image CVE
# scan and the filesystem (dependency) scan in .github/workflows/security.yml.
#
# The image-scan gate FAILS the build on any unignored HIGH/CRITICAL finding.
# An entry here is an explicit, auditable decision to accept a specific CVE for
# now. Keep it small; prefer upgrading the dependency over ignoring.
#
# RULES for every exception (enforced by review, not tooling):
#   1. One CVE id per line (e.g. CVE-2024-XXXXX or GHSA-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx).
#   2. Immediately above it, a comment block with THREE fields:
#        Justification: why this CVE is not exploitable / not fixable here.
#        Added / Review date: YYYY-MM-DD when accepted; YYYY-MM-DD to re-check.
#        Owner: who signed off.
#   3. Re-review on or before the review date; drop the entry once a fix ships.
#
# Example (commented out — this is the required shape, not an active ignore):
#
#   # Justification: stdlib net/http CVE only reachable via the HTTP/2 server
#   #   path; the operator runs no inbound HTTP server, only the webhook which
#   #   is fronted by the API server. Not exploitable in our deployment.
#   # Added: 2026-11-05  Review: 2026-12-05
#   # Owner: DevOps Engineer (ISI-7120)
#   CVE-2024-00000
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Booth API (ISI-7149) residual golang.org/x/* advisories — ride the ISI-7128
# toolchain remediation.
#
# These are transitive deps of k8s client-go v0.31.0 / controller-runtime
# v0.19.0 in the new booth/ module. We FIRST upgraded every one we could
# without a go-directive bump, which genuinely cleared several (incl. the one
# advisory govulncheck flagged as reachable at the originally-pinned versions):
#   - golang.org/x/oauth2 -> v0.27.0  (clears CVE-2025-22868, HIGH)
#   - golang.org/x/net    -> v0.40.0  (clears CVE-2024-45338, CVE-2025-22870,
#                                      CVE-2025-22872 — incl. the reachable
#                                      IPv6-zone proxy-bypass)
#   - golang.org/x/crypto -> v0.38.0  (clears CVE-2025-22869)
#
# The CVEs listed below are what REMAINS. Their fixes require x/net >=0.60
# (go 1.26) and x/crypto/x/text >=0.52/0.41 (go 1.25). That go directive is
# incompatible with the repo-pinned golangci-lint v1.61 (ci.yml / booth-ci.yml
# quality job) — the exact toolchain coupling the operator defers to ISI-7128
# (go1.26.10 + x/net v0.62.0). `govulncheck` shows the residual reachable ones
# are all in this same go-1.23 stdlib + x/net-via-client-go surface that the
# operator's own govulncheck/image-scan gates are ALREADY ratcheted against for
# the identical reason. Booth rides that same remediation: drop this block when
# ISI-7128 lands (tracked by the ISI-7142 ratchet re-arm), bumping both modules
# + golangci-lint together.
# Added: 2026-11-06  Review: 2026-12-06
# Owner: Claude Code (ISI-7149); pending board acceptance on PR #18
#
